Programming Format
Header:
It is best practice to put the following block at the start of your program:
g90g72g94f300
g90=absolute; g72=diameter; g94=ipm; f300=fastest cutting speed
A brief description and setup instructions in (comment blocks) may be put at the top of your 
program.
Comments are any text or data enclosed in parentheses“( )”. 
Their purpose is to convey to the operator any information that the programmer might think is 
useful. Comments are displayed in the center of the screen. They stay on the screen until the 
comment is changed. To clear the previous comment put blank parentheses ().
Keep the amount of text to a minimum, too much text can cause problems. 
A good place to put comments is on a line with a tool call ie: T1(LH turn tool)
Use only text, do not use periods or commas or any other symbol.
Do not put any comments in a loop.
Commas are not allowed anywhere in the program
