Notes on use:
The C-Axis is fully coordinated with the X & Z axes; the CNC sees it as a third linear axis. Simply 
program how far in Z and/or X the slide should move for a given angular rotation in C and the CNC 
will calculate the necessary feed rates.
Jogging and setting Custom Home Position:
Refer to 1.14 for location of Jog control.
To enable the C-Axis, press Alt-C (press and hold the Alt key, then press the “C” key); the
spindle will rotate to its home position and lock.
The spindle can be manually positioned with the C-Axis Jog control. Slow, medium and fast rota tion is accomplished by choosing 1, 2 or 3; incremental rotation is accomplished by choosing 4 - 8.
